parameters.text:
=Research this topic thoroughly for an educational piece:

TOPIC: {{ $json.topic }}
KEYWORDS: {{ $json.keywords }}
CONTENT TYPE: {{ $json.content_type }}

Find current facts, statistics, expert perspectives, and concrete examples. Use both tools available to you — Tavily for current/live information, Wikipedia for foundational background.

=Write the complete {{ $('⚙️ Set Inputs').item.json.content_type }} now for {{ $('⚙️ Set Inputs').item.json.platform }}.

TOPIC: {{ $('⚙️ Set Inputs').item.json.topic }}
TARGET LENGTH: {{ $('⚙️ Set Inputs').item.json.word_count }} words
KEYWORDS TO WEAVE IN NATURALLY: {{ $('⚙️ Set Inputs').item.json.keywords }}

RESEARCH TO DRAW FROM (cite facts inline as markdown links [Title](URL)):
{{ $json.output }}

Start immediately — no preamble, no "Here is..." framing.

parameters.jsCode:
const cfg = $('⚙️ Set Inputs').item.json;
const humanized = ($input.first().json.output || '').trim();
const researchRaw = $('🔍 Research Agent').item.json.output || '';

let sources = '_No structured sources returned — verify claims manually._';
const split = researchRaw.split(/###\s*SOURCES/i);
if (split.length > 1) {
  sources = split[1].trim();
}

const date = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
const wordCount = humanized.split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).length;

const finalMarkdown = `# ${cfg.topic}\n\n*By ${cfg.author_name} · ${date} · Platform: ${cfg.platform}*\n\n---\n\n${humanized}\n\n---\n\n## Sources\n\n${sources}\n`;

return [{
  json: {
    title: cfg.topic,
    author: cfg.author_name,
    platform: cfg.platform,
    content_type: cfg.content_type,
    humanizer_intensity: cfg.humanizer_intensity,
    word_count: wordCount,
    generated_date: date,
    final_markdown: finalMarkdown
  }
}];
